{
  "case_id": "2021-20-493",
  "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BRANT C. MARTIN, ESQUIRE, Fort Worth, Texas; on behalf of the Petitioners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question this case presents is whether the Restoration Act subjects the Pueblo to Texas's time, place, and manner restrictions as it relates to games that Texas does not flatly prohibit. It does not. In the Restoration Act, Congress codified the Cabazon Band framework and specifically foreclosed Texas's regulatory authority over the tribe's gaming activities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Is there any difference -- where -- is there a grant of jurisdiction in 107(a)?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All gaming activities which are prohibited by the laws of the State of Texas are hereby prohibited on the reservation and on the lands of the tribes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Martin",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Texas Bingo Enabling Act, as you're referencing, it's specific charitable organizations, Your Honor, that are -- that are set forth in that regulatory scheme."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So why is this not prohibited if it's not a charitable organization?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just six months after this Court drew the distinction in Cabazon under Public Law 280 between gaming activity that is prohibited versus gaming activity that is regulated by state law, Congress enacted Section 107, mirroring that language to draw the same distinction in the exact same Indian gaming context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And what would be the negative consequences in the government's view, if any, if we were to elide this distinction, ignore it, overrule Cabazon?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I'd love to hear what the difference between bingo and dingo is, so please."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Didn't the tribal resolution ask that the statute include \"language which would provide that all gambling\" -- \"gaming, gambling, lottery, or bingo, as defined by the laws and administrative regulations of the State of Texas, shall be prohibited on the tribe's reservation or on tribal land\"? Didn't it say that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pettit (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, it ignores that when it comes to gambling, the Restoration Act departs from the Cabazon Band framework by treating both civil and criminal penalties and civil and criminal regulatory jurisdiction the same way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pettit (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Second, it overlooks that the Cabazon Band test was written to avoid a form of state encroachment into tribal affairs that isn't possible when a federal court is applying federal law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pettit (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: So prohibition in this context and as generally understood can include a regulation except for, as Justice Barrett noted a couple of times, Cabazon Band."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pettit (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: By looking at the context of each of the statutes, each of the statutes they cite is a settlement act that is enabling a preexisting agreement between the parties to litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pettit (Respondent)",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: Yes, Your Honor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Wouldn't that logic seem to suggest, if that's true, then -- then -- then Cabazon, we should just get rid of it and scrap it and -- and the consequences for IGRA be damned?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. PETTIT",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: No, Your Honor, that's not necessary in this case because, as my opposing counsel has conceded, this is about federalizing state law, and Cabazon doesn't -- specifically declined to address that question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But -- but, Ms. Pettit, why is it uniquely unworkable in this context?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. PETTIT",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: So the lower courts have suggested that Mr. Yang is incorrect on that point, that, in fact, it's difficult to derive a single rule between what is prohibitory and what is regulatory precisely because many of the things that are nominally prohibitory are very close -- very close concerns of state public policy, so they just don't track."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, isn't that an argument for overturning it in IGRA too and just getting rid of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. PETTIT",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. PETTIT: So IGRA incorporated a specific part of Cabazon Band that allows the tribe in 2710 to engage in Class II gaming, which permits them to -- if the state permits it under any person, any purpose, any organization."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b2bddc0e0389-0004-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 94,
        "start": 94
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Suppose you scrapped your laws about bingo and you enacted a statute that says that under specified circumstances, a type of gambling called Texas Traditional Board Game is allowed, and you defined that involving a board and et cetera, et cetera. But this is not bingo. This is the Traditional Texas Board Game. Then would bingo be prohibited, or would it be regulated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-493",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "b2bddc0e03890ddd83f12ea2586917ae74028ce68a99fe74a2563491c2278c05",
